ralph/prd.json:2756:      "notes": "Implemented: PATCH /v1/organizations/{org_id}/limits upserts organization-scoped quota policies. Request body: {limits:[{resource,limit_value,enforcement_mode?}, ...]} validated by httpapi (missing limit_value -> 400) and by the store layer (closed-set resource, non-negative limit, closed-set mode, no duplicates). Required action limits.write (CapAdmin, no support cross-tenant exception). Store-layer LimitsService composes a tenant existence pre-check (typed NotFound on missing org), one organization-scoped quota_policies upsert per entry, an immutable audit record (action=limits.write, metadata.updated_resources=sorted closed-set names), and an in-tx re-read of effective limits — all in one Store.Write. New QuotaRepository.UpsertOrganizationPolicy uses ON CONFLICT (organization_id, resource) WHERE scope_kind='organization' to target the partial unique index. Wired through NewHandler/newRouteTable as a new LimitsUpdater port; the route uses organizationIDResolver so cross-tenant {org_id} is a 403 before the handler runs. cmd/yalla-api builds the LimitsService at startup."
ralph/prd.json:7069:      "notes": "Real-quota concurrent oversubscription integration test at internal/controlplane/store/environment_quota_concurrent_test.go — first BE-0323-pattern clone (environments dimension). Wires real *store.EnvironmentService over real *quota.Checker/*store.QuotaRepository/quota.StaticPlanResolver/*store.AuditRepository; uses local race-safe atomicAuthorizer/atomicJobs (shared recordingAuthorizer/recordingJobs use plain int counters whose -race-with-DB failure is a pre-existing triage item documented in progress.txt). 20 goroutines × limit=5 → exactly 5 successes, 15 E_QUOTA_EXCEEDED rejections carrying ExceededDetail{Resource=environments,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; environments table row count, active quota_reservations count, and QuotaRepository.SumActiveReservations through Store.Read all == 5; authz.calls==20, jobs.calls==5 pins authorize→quota.Reserve→write→jobs.Enqueue step order at the unit-of-work level. Pre-existing factory id-prefix bug surfaced (testutil.Factory.Project uses 'prj_' but domain.KindProject is 'proj'); test bypasses with raw SQL + domain.MustNewID like seedDomainOrg. gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./..., go test -race ./..., and focused -race against live Postgres all pass."
ralph/prd.json:7107:      "notes": "Quota dimension: applications (per-subtype). Service.Create now reserves TWO dimensions in the same DB transaction when Kind == ServiceKindApplication — the existing QuotaResourceServices reservation (BE-0325) and the new QuotaResourceApplications reservation. Non-application kinds (compose, database) do NOT consume the applications dimension. New integration tests at internal/controlplane/store/service_quota_applications_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestServiceServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForApplicationsQuota — 20 goroutines × applications limit=5 with a loose services limit=40 prove the applications row lock serialises concurrent application creates; rejections carry ExceededDetail{Resource=applications,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; service rows, active applications reservations, and active services reservations all == 5; (2) TestServiceServiceCreateAppliesApplicationsQuotaOnlyToApplicationKind — after exhausting the applications dimension with 5 application-kind services, a 6th application Create is rejected on applications while a compose-kind and a database-kind Create both succeed and only consume the services dimension. Pre-existing TestAPIKeyServiceCreate* and TestOrganizationVariableServicePatch* failures unchanged (factory id/slug-vs-ParseSlug issue documented under BE-0127 / BE-0324). gofmt, go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./..., and YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestServiceServiceCreate(Rejects|Applies)' ./internal/controlplane/store/ all pass."
ralph/prd.json:7164:      "notes": "Quota dimension: domains. ServiceDomainService.Create now reserves one unit on QuotaResourceDomains inside the same *Tx as the in-transaction authorize, the Insert, and the audit append (BE-0329). NewServiceDomainService gains a QuotaReserver dependency; cmd/yalla-api/main.go passes the existing serviceQuota placeholder until the real quota.Checker is wired into the HTTP layer. New integration tests at internal/controlplane/store/service_domain_quota_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestServiceDomainServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForDomainsQuota — 20 goroutines x domains limit=5 prove the domains row lock serialises concurrent domain creates; rejections carry ExceededDetail{Resource=domains,Limit=5,Requested=1,Reserved=5,Current=0}; service_domains rows == 5; active domains reservations == 5; rejection diagnostic carries no caller hostname/request_id/correlation_id/domain_id leakage; (2) TestServiceDomainServiceCreateAppliesDomainsQuotaIndependentlyOfServicesQuota — after exhausting the domains dimension a 6th domain Create is rejected on the domains dimension and the services dimension is never touched (0 active services reservations). Pre-existing TestEnvironmentServiceCreateQuotaFailureRollsBack and TestOrganizationVariableServicePatchValueOnlyPreservesIsSecret failures unchanged (unrelated, documented under BE-0127 / BE-0324). gofmt, go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./..., and YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run \"TestServiceDomainServiceCreate(Rejects|Applies)\" ./internal/controlplane/store/ all pass."
ralph/prd.json:7278:      "notes": "Quota dimension: monthly_deployments. DeploymentService.Create and DeploymentService.Rollback both reserve monthly_deployments AFTER concurrent_deployments inside the same *Tx as the in-tx Authorize, the deployment row Insert, the provisioning-job Enqueue, and the audit Append — so a rejection on either dimension rolls the entire unit of work back. The constant QuotaResourceMonthlyDeployments and its DOMAIN membership were already in place from BE-0006 (migration 0006_quota_policy_schema.up.sql) and the in-source quota_internal_test.go count-equality guard, so no new migration was needed. Two new concurrent integration tests in internal/controlplane/store/deployment_quota_monthly_deployments_concurrent_test.go: RejectsParallelOversubscription (20 goroutines × monthly_deployments=5 → 5 successes, 15 typed CodeQuotaExceeded rejections whose ExceededDetail.Resource is monthly_deployments, Limit=5, Requested=1, Reserved=5, Current=0; rejection messages do not echo idempotency_key, request_id, correlation_id, or source_ref; deployments row count and active monthly_deployments reservations both equal 5; concurrent_deployments reservations stay at 0 because no policy is seeded for that dimension; SumActiveReservations agrees with raw count; authorizer.calls = 20 proves authorize ran on every attempt; jobs.calls = 5 proves enqueue ran only on winners, pinning the authorize→quota→insert→enqueue order under contention); AppliesIndependently (exhaust serially, sixth Create rejects on monthly_deployments specifically — never another dimension — and no concurrent_deployments or services reservation is ever taken)."
ralph/prd.json:7297:      "notes": "Quota dimension: concurrent_deployments. Call sites for Reserve(concurrent_deployments) were already in place inside DeploymentService.Create and DeploymentService.Rollback (reserved FIRST in both unit-of-work transactions, before monthly_deployments). This story added the BE-0336 focused concurrent integration tests in internal/controlplane/store/deployment_quota_concurrent_deployments_concurrent_test.go: (1) TestDeploymentServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionForConcurrentDeploymentsQuota races 20 goroutines against a hard-enforced concurrent_deployments limit of 5, with monthly_deployments intentionally unpoliced; asserts exactly 5 successes / 15 rejections, every rejection carries CodeQuotaExceeded with ExceededDetail.Resource=concurrent_deployments and Limit=5/Requested=1/Reserved=5/Current=0, the diagnostic string leaks no idempotency_key/request_id/correlation_id/source_ref, exactly 5 deployment rows exist in the (org, service) scope, exactly 5 active concurrent_deployments reservations exist, zero monthly_deployments reservations exist (proves the unpoliced sibling never accumulates rows), SumActiveReservations agrees with the raw count, and the JobEnqueuer call count equals the success count (proving the Reserve is positioned before the Enqueue). (2) TestDeploymentServiceCreateAppliesConcurrentDeploymentsQuotaIndependentlyOfMonthlyDeployments is the negative complement: it exhausts concurrent_deployments by creating 5 deployments serially, then proves a 6th Create rejects on the concurrent_deployments dimension specifically (never disguised as monthly_deployments), and that the unpoliced monthly_deployments and unrelated services dimensions accumulate zero reservation rows. Verification: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go build clean, go test ./... PASS, go test -race ./... PASS, focused BE-0336 tests PASS (1.758s) under -race against real Postgres, full TestDeploymentService|backup|cpu|memory|storage sweep PASS (2.994s) under -race -parallel=2 against real Postgres."
ralph/prd.json:9140:      "notes": "Database table: api_keys. Added internal/controlplane/store/api_key_repository_invariants_test.go (11 t.Parallel tests) covering the BE-0427/BE-0429/BE-0431 invariants-file template adapted for api_keys (no version column, three distinct UPDATE paths, secret-bearing row body): Insert returns row with non-zero created_at == updated_at, nil lifecycle stamps, and verbatim credential primitives; UpdateMutable / Revoke / RotateCredential / TouchLastUsed each anchor the trigger dual-anchor (created_at preserved, updated_at refreshed by api_keys_set_updated_at); RotateCredential additionally pins identity / ownership / scopes / lifecycle preservation plus FindByPrefix re-binding to the new prefix and NotFound on the old one; UpdateMutable pins the {name, scopes} mutable surface with byte-identical non-mutable columns; Insert-rolls-back additionally proves the secret-bearing extension — no row anywhere in api_keys carries the rolled-back secret_hash OR prefix (the credential primitives that survive an autonomous-transaction refactor even when Get-by-id reports NotFound); nil-Tx guards on all five mutation paths render typed apierr.Internal (the pre-existing TestAPIKeyRepositoryInsertRejectsNilTx only asserted err != nil). gofmt, go vet, focused TestAPIKeyRepository run, and race-detector run on the new tests all pass. Pre-existing parallel-test flakes (TestRequireDBIsParallelSafe/worker-N, TestService*ServiceCreateRejectsParallelOversubscriptionFor*Quota) under full-suite go test ./... are Postgres max_connections exhaustion documented in BE-0428..BE-0432 progress entries; both pass when run in isolation."
