ralph/prd.json:9482:      "notes": "Repository-level invariants for QuotaRepository's quota_policies write surface and ListEffectiveLimits resolver landed in internal/controlplane/store/quota_policy_repository_invariants_test.go. UpsertOrganizationPolicy is now pinned for: INSERT row shape (id qpol_<token>, scope_kind='organization', plan IS NULL, organization_id=$1, timestamps set, updated_at - created_at <= 1s); UPDATE branch preserves id and created_at byte-equal and refreshes updated_at via the set_updated_at trigger; org override never touches the plan_default row (id/limit/mode/created_at/updated_at byte-equal across the upsert); FK violation on unknown organization_id surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict through mapWriteError; negative limit_value rejected by the CHECK as Conflict; unknown enforcement_mode rejected by the DOMAIN as Conflict; every EnforcementMode constant (hard/soft/metered/disabled) round-trips. ListEffectiveLimits is pinned for: deterministic alpha resource order with override-beats-default per resource; tenant scoping (orgB never sees orgA's overrides and only sees plan defaults for its own plan); plan isolation (a 'pro' default does not bleed into a 'starter' read); empty result when neither scope is configured. UpsertOrganizationPolicy rollback proven via a typed sentinel returned from the Store.Write closure (errors.Is(err, sentinel) and EffectiveLimit reports unconfigured after). nil-tx guard returns yerr.CodeInternal. Per-resource EffectiveLimit semantics remain owned by the existing quota_repository_test.go; schema-level uniqueness/scope-consistency/cascade invariants remain owned by quota_schema_test.go. gofmt, go mod tidy, go vet ./..., the focused TestQuotaRepository{Upsert,ListEffectiveLimits}* run, and the same subset under -race all pass. Three pre-existing failures (TestEnvironmentRepoGetByIDReturnsRow, TestEnvironmentRepoListByProjectReturnsDeterministicOrdering, TestProjectVariableServiceReplaceCrossTenantProjectIsNotFound) reproduce at HEAD without this change and are unrelated to BE-0451."
