diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index c299092bc9416b3e3738f1f3d927923301adf798..bab75003bd58f02e0f83882814a311f316cb460d
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Pricing plan catalog rows are versioned, global configuration rather than tenant data: `plans` uses immutable accepted versions keyed by `(slug, billing_period, version)` plus one active version per `(slug, billing_period)`, and `PricingPlanRepository.Update` archives the addressed row before inserting the next version and cloning entitlements. Do not update an accepted plan row in place.
 - Database engine drift is a service subtype mismatch in reconciliation: when both desired and actual are `dokploy.ServiceDatabase` but `Engine` differs after trim/case normalization, emit one dangerous `ActionReviewServiceTypeChange` / `ReasonServiceTypeChanged` action and return before env/domain safe repairs. This prevents auto-mutating a database resource whose storage engine no longer matches Yalla source of truth.
 - `E_INTERNAL` is the backend's generic programming/unexpected-failure contract: use `apierr.Internal(cause)`, render HTTP 500, keep the public message fixed as "an unexpected internal error occurred", omit public hints/details, preserve the cause only for server-side logging, and keep nil-error envelope fallback on the same message/docs-link contract.
 - Reconciliation service-type mismatches are dangerous review-only drift: once desired and actual `dokploy.ServiceType` differ, `diffService` must emit `ActionReviewServiceTypeChange` and stop before build/env/domain safe repairs. Safe repairs against an untrusted upstream type can mutate the wrong Dokploy resource shape.

diff --git a/internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md b/internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md
index 2b06ad10a31a0340613fed4288ac961d8101c784..d63a3d6972a4c5318d104c4f5399740b3f36c024
--- a/internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md
+++ b/internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md
@@ -259,6 +259,23 @@
   Quota accounting rows (`quota_usage`, `quota_reservations`) are **not** domain
   resources — `newQuotaID` mints their ids locally, no `domain.Kind`.
 
+## Pricing plans (`0049_pricing_plan_catalog`, `pricing_plan.go`)
+
+- `plans` is global pricing configuration, not tenant-owned customer data. It
+  carries a versioned package contract: `(slug, billing_period, version)` is
+  unique, and only one row may be `active` for a `(slug, billing_period)` pair.
+  Future subscriptions should reference the accepted plan row, not only the
+  slug, so audits can recover the exact accepted package after later changes.
+- Do not mutate an accepted plan row in place. `PricingPlanRepository.Update`
+  locks the current row, archives it, inserts the next version, and clones the
+  existing `plan_entitlements` rows onto the new version in the same
+  transaction. Change entitlements on the new version with
+  `UpsertEntitlement`.
+- `plan_entitlements.enforcement_mode` reuses `quota_enforcement_mode`
+  (`hard`, `soft`, `metered`, `disabled`) but uses a free-form
+  `entitlement_key` because billing-grade metrics extend beyond the current
+  `quota_resource` domain. Keys must stay value-free and non-secret.
+
 ## Service lifecycle (`0041_service_state_machine`, `service.go`, `service_event.go`)
 
 - `services.status` is the source-of-truth lifecycle state for the service row
