diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index c299092bc9416b3e3738f1f3d927923301adf798..51a66442df4c2b2009e2936296acd92e950058e0
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Pricing plan catalog rows are versioned, global configuration rather than tenant data: `plans` uses immutable accepted versions keyed by `(slug, billing_period, version)` plus one active version per `(slug, billing_period)`, and `PricingPlanRepository.Update` archives the addressed row before inserting the next version and cloning entitlements. Do not update an accepted plan row in place.
 - Database engine drift is a service subtype mismatch in reconciliation: when both desired and actual are `dokploy.ServiceDatabase` but `Engine` differs after trim/case normalization, emit one dangerous `ActionReviewServiceTypeChange` / `ReasonServiceTypeChanged` action and return before env/domain safe repairs. This prevents auto-mutating a database resource whose storage engine no longer matches Yalla source of truth.
 - `E_INTERNAL` is the backend's generic programming/unexpected-failure contract: use `apierr.Internal(cause)`, render HTTP 500, keep the public message fixed as "an unexpected internal error occurred", omit public hints/details, preserve the cause only for server-side logging, and keep nil-error envelope fallback on the same message/docs-link contract.
 - Reconciliation service-type mismatches are dangerous review-only drift: once desired and actual `dokploy.ServiceType` differ, `diffService` must emit `ActionReviewServiceTypeChange` and stop before build/env/domain safe repairs. Safe repairs against an untrusted upstream type can mutate the wrong Dokploy resource shape.
@@ -36558,3 +36559,14 @@
   - Mongo drift reconciliation uses the shared database subtype path: `ServiceDatabase` plus `EngineMongo`, with engine drift classified as `ActionReviewServiceTypeChange` / `ReasonServiceTypeChanged` before any env/domain repair.
   - Database-engine reconciliation verification remains a mechanical clone of the postgres/mysql/mariadb pattern; keep classification fields value-free and route secrets only through repairer-only fields.
 ---
+## 2026-05-19 05:08 +03 - BE-0563
+- What was implemented: Added the versioned pricing plan catalog schema and repository. Migration `0049_pricing_plan_catalog` creates `plans`, `plan_entitlements`, `pricing_plan_status`, and `pricing_billing_period`; seeds Starter, Pro, Business, and Enterprise monthly v1 packages; and seeds entitlements covering hard, soft, metered, and disabled enforcement modes. `PricingPlanRepository` now supports create, exact-version reads, active listing, update-by-archive-and-new-version, archive, entitlement upsert, and entitlement listing.
+- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0049_pricing_plan_catalog.up.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0049_pricing_plan_catalog.down.sql`, `internal/controlplane/store/pricing_plan.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/pricing_plan_internal_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/pricing_plan_schema_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/pricing_plan_repository_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/store/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
+- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`; `docker compose up -d postgres`; `YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -count=1 -run 'TestMigrations|TestPricingPlan|TestBuildPlan' ./internal/controlplane/store ./internal/controlplane/store/migrate`; `YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestPricingPlan|TestBuildPlan' ./internal/controlplane/store`.
+- Results: All required and focused checks passed. `golangci-lint` passed with 0 issues. `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` are not installed in this environment, so those optional checks could not be run.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: No HTTP route was added in this schema story, so public JSON envelope and route-level authorization criteria remain for the pricing admin/customer API stories. Future subscription stories should reference the accepted `plans.id`/`version`, not only the slug.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Pricing plans are global versioned configuration, not tenant-owned rows; accepted versions are retained by archiving rather than in-place mutation.
+  - `PricingPlanRepository.Update` must close the entitlement read cursor before writing cloned entitlements in the same transaction; pgx transactions cannot run another statement while rows from the previous query are still open.
+  - `plan_entitlements` intentionally uses free-form `entitlement_key` with `quota_enforcement_mode` because pricing/metering dimensions extend beyond the existing `quota_resource` domain.
+---

